The current-visit assessment/plan (item 2) documents "Chronic kidney disease stage 3a due to type 2 diabetes." This is an explicit causal link made by the treating provider on the date of service. It is supported by eGFR 56, albuminuria (UACR 232), and management with lisinopril and dapagliflozin plus a BMP in 3 months. The face-to-face visit was with an acceptable provider type, so E11.22 (with N18.31) is supported.

The "prior visit summary" carries a similar statement, but the current assessment independently documents it, so the code does not rely on that section.

