The note documents Type 1 diabetes, not Type 2, so E11.22 is not supported. The correct code family would be E10.22 (Type 1 diabetes with diabetic chronic kidney disease), plus N18.31. Even that pairing is uncertain: the note never explicitly links the CKD to diabetes, although ICD-10-CM's "with" convention would generally presume the link. Because the diabetes type is Type 1 throughout, E11.22 fails.

The note has other inconsistencies. It mentions an insulin pump in the plan, but the medications list injections (glargine and lispro). That does not change the conclusion for E11.22.

